2026.\n\nDuring Q2'2026, average property prices for Swayam Rudra Heights moved from ₹ 22,150/sqft to ₹ 30,200/sqft, reflecting a 36.34% rise.\n\n#### MMRDA Presents Surplus Budget with Significant Allocation for Infrastructure\n\nMMRDA has presented a surplus budget of ₹48,072 crore, with 87% allocated to infrastructure projects, including roads, public transport, and urban development. A notable provision of ₹4,000 crore is earmarked for the development of Mumbai 3.0 New Town, aiming for planned urban expansion.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### Mumbai-Pune Expressway 'Missing Link' Project Set for May 1 Inauguration, Promising Safer and Faster Travel\n\nThe highly anticipated 'Missing Link' project on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway is set to be inaugurated on May 1, significantly reducing travel time by approximately 30 minutes and enhancing safety. The 10.5-km stretch features tunnels and a bridge, bypassing the accident-prone Khandala Ghat. This infrastructure upgrade is expected to ease traffic congestion, improve travel safety.\n\nDuring Q1'2026, average property prices for Swayam Rudra Heights moved from ₹ 21,050/sqft to ₹ 22,150/sqft, reflecting a 5.23% rise.\n\nStructural Works reach 80% completion. External Works has reached 100%. Internal finishing stands at 100%. MEP Services including lift and staircases, are now 93% done\n\nA total of 15 out of 24 launched units have been booked as of August 2023, including 62% of 2 BHK(13 out of 21 units), 100% of 1 BHK(2 units).\n\nA total of 14 out of 25 launched units have been booked as of June 2022, including 50% of 1 BHK(1 out of 2 units), 62% of 2 BHK(13 out of 21 units).\n\n### Gov